t;confidence&quot;: &quot;high&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Section present in the page&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;F-2&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: 2, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Opening hours are listed&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;low&quot;, &quot;confidence&quot;: &quot;high&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Section present in the page&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;F-3&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: 3, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;The address and a map link are shown&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;low&quot;, &quot;confidence&quot;: &quot;high&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Section present in the page&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;F-4&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: 4, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Visitors can pre-order a coffee for pickup with a form&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;low&quot;, &quot;confidence&quot;: &quot;high&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Section present in the page&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;F-5&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: 5, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Layout works on a phone&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;low&quot;, &quot;confidence&quot;: &quot;high&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Viewport meta tag present; layout is fluid&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;R-1&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: &quot;R-1&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Consistent styling: the whole page follows the style guide (same fonts, colours, button and card styles)&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;medium&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Mock: looks fine in the measurements&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;R-2&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: &quot;R-2&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Readable contrast: text is easy to read against its background (WCAG AA)&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;medium&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Mock: looks fine in the measurements&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;R-3&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: &quot;R-3&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Clear hierarchy: one main heading, headings in order, the most important things stand out&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;medium&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Mock: looks fine in the measurements&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;R-4&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: &quot;R-4&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;One obvious main action: a visitor can tell at once what to do next&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;medium&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Mock: looks fine in the measurements&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;R-5&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: &quot;R-5&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Easy navigation: a visitor can reach every section quickly, on a phone too&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;medium&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Mock: looks fine in the measurements&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;R-6&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: &quot;R-6&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Tap targets are big enough on phones (at least 44x44px)&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;medium&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Mock: looks fine in the measurements&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;: &quot;R-7&quot;, &quot;item&quot;: &quot;R-7&quot;, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Images have alt text&quot;, &quot;verdict&quot;: &quot;PASS&quot;, &quot;severity&quot;: &quot;medium&quot;, &quot;note&quot;: &quot;Mock: looks fine in the measurements&quot;}]\nWORKABLE CHECK BY CODE: not workable: [&quot;necessary condition N2 not met: No JavaScript errors on load (could not run: Chrome not found (set J2_CHROME); no render or script run.)&quot;, &quot;necessary condition N3 not met: No horizontal overflow at 360px and 1280px (could not run: Chrome not found (set J2_CHROME); no render or script run.)&quot;, &quot;render check didn't run, so JS errors, overflow and forms are unverified: Chrome not found (set J2_CHROME); no render or script run.&quot;]\nFACTS ONLY THE REQUESTER KNOWS (from Audit): []\n\nJ2.h: the site is done only when it is workable: every done-when item passes Audit, no JS errors, no horizontal overflow at 360px and 1280px, forms work, no broken in-page link, every necessary condition met, nothing to be confirmed. Code checks this. Workable: declare done=true and tell the Requester the goal is reached. Not workable: it goes back to Adaptation (J2.b); give the instruction. If a fix needs a fact only the Requester knows (facts above, or any you see), set needs_requester=true and ask for it in requester_questions; the run pauses until they answer. Never offer adding budget, leaving items out or finishing as is in your own question: set needs_decision instead and code asks the Requester with the exact amounts it can apply.\nWHEN YOU WRITE TO THE REQUESTER (any say addressed to them, any question or option for them): they are a college student with no tech background. Use everyday words. Never use internal terms: charter, done-when, checklist, standards, reserve, fix, effort, budget, units, workflow, cycle, finding, audit, ruling, envelope, content types such as &quot;warmth content&quot;, or the names of the functions (Identity, Adaptation, Priority, Coordination, Audit). At most two short sentences of context. Each option says what they get and what it costs, in plain words, e.g. &quot;Add a gallery of past work (takes a bit longer)&quot; / &quot;Keep it simple, no gallery&quot;. No recommendation.</pre></div><div class=\"adrow\"><b>raw output</b><pre class=\"arttext\">{&quot;to_requester&quot;: &quot;&quot;, &quot;to_agents&quot;: &quot;@Adaptation Not workable yet; the failing findings need rework.&quot;, &quot;clause&quot;: &quot;done_when&quot;, &quot;done&quot;: false, &quot;needs_requester&quot;: false, &quot;requester_questions&quot;: [], &quot;next&quot;: &quot;Adaptation&quot;}</pre></div></details></details><details class=\"adcall\" data-call=\"26\"><summary>Call 3 · step 8 · cycle 2 · 0 s · 10:00:04</summary><div class=\"adrow\"><b>Was given</b> the charter (Brew Lab: 5 checklist items), the workflow list (6 registered: W-1 done, W-2 done, W-3 done, W-4 done, W-5 done, W-6 done), Audit's findings (audit of v5: 5/5 pass), the chat (46 messages), its task</div><div class=\"adrow\"><b>Reason</b> <p>Scripted mock reply: no model reasoning.</p></div><div class=\"adrow\"><b>Reply</b> <p class=\"empty\">(sent as its message to You (the Requester))</p></div><details class=\"adtech\"><summary>Show technical details</summary><div class=\"adrow\"><b>system text</b><pre class=\"arttext\">&lt;!-- PLACEHOLDER written from the J2 page and the J2 flow diagram (docs/j2-flow.jpg). Replace with the official file when it arrives. --&gt;\n# Department rules (every function follows these)\n\nYou are one of five functions running one department in Native: Identity, Adaptation, Priority,\nCoordination and Audit. Each registered workflow gets its own workflow agent (&quot;W-1 Builder&quot;, &quot;W-2 Builder&quot;, ...)\nthat runs only that workflow and owns one marked section of the site file. A code validator checks the charter and each\nworkflow before it is registered. The Requester (a person) gives the brief, answers Identity's questions and\nmay ask for changes at the end. There is no CEO: where a role file says &quot;ask the CEO&quot;, Identity asks the\nRequester instead, and no other function may. The department's job right now is to build the website the\nRequester asked for.\n\n## How we work\n- Everyone reads the whole chat and the current goal before speaking. Keep messages short: 1-3 sentences.\n- Address others by @name: @Identity, @Adaptation, @Priority, @Coordination, @Audit, or a workflow agent\n  by its id (@W-1).\n- Only Identity talks to the Requester (@Requester). If you need something from the Requester, tell\n  @Identity; code redirects any other message to the Requester to Identity.\n- Identity's goal and &quot;done when&quot; list are the reference for every decision.\n- Disagree with a reason tied to the goal, the budget or the standards. Don't give in just to be nice,\n  but move when someone gives a better reason.\n- Any two functions that disagree (Adaptation and Priority over funding, Adaptation and Audit over a finding,\n  Adaptation and Coordination over a HOLD) try to settle it themselves within 4 attempts. If they can't, it\n  goes to Identity with both final positions. Identity rules from the charter; if the charter doesn't decide\n  it, Identity asks the Requester one decision-ready question, then rules.\n- A missing fact only the Requester knows becomes a question from Identity to the Requester. If the Requester\n  can't supply it yet, it is &quot;to be confirmed&quot; and that done-when item is not met.\n- The work isn't finished until the site is workable: every done-when item passes Audit, no JavaScript\n  errors, no horizontal overflow at 360px and 1280px, forms work, no broken in-page link, nothing to be\n  confirmed. Until then the loop J2.b to J2.h repeats. When a safety limit is hit (budget, cycles, the same\n  failure twice in a row), Identity asks the Requester to add budget, drop the item or ship as is.\n- The website is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript in one file (CDN libraries are fine). No build step.\n\n## The flow (J2.a to J2.h)\nJ2.a Identity: enough information to work? If not, ask the Requester and wait, as many rounds as needed.\nThen record the charter. J2.b Adaptation proposes workflows, using relevant lessons from earlier work.\nJ2.c Priority prices them: GRANT, COUNTER (Adaptation revises) or REFUSE (Adaptation reshapes or parks it);\nthe bargain is bounded by four hops, fifteen minutes and its spend. J2.d Identity resolves what the agents\ncouldn't. J2.e The validator checks and registers the workflow and creates its agent (rejected: Adaptation\nreshapes or parks it). J2.f Coordination schedules and holds the write lock; Priority checks each run's\nenvelope (over limit: hold it, or request approval from Identity); the workflow's agent runs it, retrying\nwithin its envelope, and reports to Coordination. J2.g Audit checks the result and files its findings to\nIdentity. J2.h Identity: is the site workable? If yes, Identity tells the Requester the goal is reached. If\nnot, back to J2.b. When Audit confirms a fix worked, Adaptation saves a lesson.\n\n## Who speaks next\nEvery reply names &quot;next&quot;. Only these hand-offs are allowed; code redirects any other pick:\n- Identity -&gt; Requester, Adaptation, Priority, Coordination or Audit\n- Adaptation -&gt; Priority; Identity for a policy question; Audit or Coordination only to dispute a finding or a HOLD\n- Priority -&gt; Adaptation; Identity once 4 exchanges are used or to request approval for a run over its envelope;\n  the workflow's agent once a run's envelope is within limits; Coordination to HOLD a run\n- Coordination -&gt; Priority (envelope check for the next run), Adaptation when everything is on HOLD\n- A workflow agent (W-n) -&gt; Coordination\n- Audit -&gt; Identity (every finding goes to Identity, who decides J2.h)\nStart your message with @&lt;next&gt;.\n\n---\nagent: identity\nrole: charter guardian and conflict closer\nreads: charter, proposals, envelope decisions, findings, alarms, recorded rules\nwrites: identity decisions, CEO questions, done verdicts\n---\n\n# Identity Agent\n\n## System instruction\n\nYou are Identity, the department's voice and constitutional authority. Keep the department aligned with its goal, done-when condition, rules and authority boundary.\n\nYou do not design workflows, allocate resources, schedule work, execute work or perform Audit. You rule only when a proposal touches policy, when Priority and Adaptation cannot agree, when Audit reports a material violation, or when the department may be done.\n\n## Your decisions\n\nYou may:\n\n- rule that a proposal is consistent or inconsistent with the charter;\n- resolve a bounded Adaptation–Priority conflict;\n- interpret an existing rule;\n- stop an unsafe or unauthorized action;\n- decide whether a material Audit finding requires rework;\n- declare that done-when holds when supported by evidence;\n- ask the CEO one decision-ready question when existing authority is insufficient.\n\nYou may not:\n\n- invent a new goal or rule;\n- choose tools or implementation steps;\n- increase an envelope;\n- choose which workflow runs first;\n- rewrite a proposal to make it acceptable;\n- ask the CEO merely because agents disagree.\n\n## Decision procedure\n\n1. Name the exact charter clause or rule that applies.\n2. Separate facts from assumptions.\n3. Decide with existing authority when possible.\n4. If the evidence is insufficient but obtainable by another function, request that evidence rather than asking the CEO.\n5. Ask the CEO only when the choice changes purpose, risk authority, external commitment or an unresolved value trade-off.\n\n## CEO question format\n\n```yaml\nmessage:\n  from: identity\n  to: CEO\n  act: ASK_CEO\n  thread: &lt;thread&gt;\n  summary: &lt;one bounded decision&gt;\n  claims:\n    - &quot;Option A: consequence, cost and risk&quot;\n    - &quot;Option B: consequence, cost and risk&quot;\n  evidence:\n    - &lt;why the charter cannot decide&gt;\n  requested_action: &quot;Choose A or B&quot;\n  blocking: true\n```\n\n## Failure patterns to avoid\n\n- Becoming a general manager who comments on every message.\n- Treating personal preference as a rule.\n- Escalating without presenting options.\n- Silently changing done-when.\n- Doing Adaptation's or Audit's work.\n\nYou are Identity.\n\n## Reply format (required)\n{&quot;say&quot;: str (to the Requester, in plain words: what has been done so far, at most 2 short sentences; don't list what is missing, code adds that list; no question, it is asked below; no recommendation; never the words &quot;building time&quot;, &quot;cap&quot;, &quot;cycles&quot;, &quot;done-when&quot; or &quot;estimate&quot;), &quot;reason&quot;: str (one short sentence: why you decided this)}</pre></div><div class=\"adrow\"><b>prompt</b><pre class=\"arttext\">STATE:\n{&quot;requester_brief&quot;: &quot;A one-page website for Brew Lab, a small specialty coffee shop in Indiranagar, Bengaluru. Visitors should see the menu with prices, the opening hours, and where to find us, and be able to pre-order a coffee for pickup. It should feel warm and modern and work well on a phone.&quot;, &quot;requester_feedback&quot;: null, &quot;charter&quot;: {&quot;statement&quot;: &quot;A one-page website for Brew Lab where visitors find what they need and come in&quot;, &quot;site_name&quot;: &quot;Brew Lab&quot;, &quot;audience&quot;: &quot;Local customers, mostly on phones&quot;, &quot;standards&quot;: [&quot;Warm, modern feel&quot;, &quot;Fast first screen on a phone&quot;], &quot;rules&quot;: [&quot;Plain HTML/CSS/JS in one file&quot;, &quot;No real customer data&quot;], &quot;done_when&quot;: [{&quot;item&quot;: 1, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;The menu with prices is shown&quot;}, {&quot;item&quot;: 2, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Opening hours are listed&quot;}, {&quot;item&quot;: 3, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;The address and a map link are shown&quot;}, {&quot;item&quot;: 4, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Visitors can pre-order a coffee for pickup with a form&quot;}, {&quot;item&quot;: 5, &quot;criterion&quot;: &quot;Layout works on a phone&quot;}], &quot;to_be_confirmed&quot;: [], &quot;dropped_from_brief&quot;: [], &quot;facts&quot;: [&quot;Brew Lab&quot;], &quot;business_type&quot;: &quot;cafe&quot;, &quot;visitor_needs&quot;: [&quot;Menu with prices&quot;, &quot;Opening hours&quot;, &quot;Where to find us&quot;], &quot;core_items&quot;: [&quot;The menu with prices is shown&quot;, &quot;Opening hours are listed&quot;, &quot;The address and a map link are shown&quot;, &quot;Visitors can